# SPA client-side routing fallback.
#
# NOTE: this also returns index.html (200) for a *missing* /assets/* hash —
# Cloudflare Pages _redirects cannot emit 404, and a self-rewrite exclusion
# (/assets/* /assets/:splat 200) was tested with `wrangler pages dev` and does
# NOT stop the fallthrough. That's why /assets/* is cached with a finite,
# self-healing max-age (see _headers) rather than `immutable`: a masquerading
# fallback must be able to expire. Stale code-split chunks after a deploy are
# handled in-session by ChunkErrorBoundary (a one-time reload).

# RFC 9116 mandates the canonical path /.well-known/security.txt; keep the
# legacy /security.txt discoverable by pointing it there. Must precede the
# catch-all below, which would otherwise swallow it into the SPA shell.
/security.txt    /.well-known/security.txt    301

/*    /index.html    200
